-- returning-lego-gwps-in-july-2026-vary-by-region
UPDATE public.news_articles SET content = $boi_t$LEGO is bringing back some previous Gifts with Purchase (GWPs) in July 2026, but here’s the catch: what you get depends entirely on where you live. This is likely a move to clear out leftover stock, which is good news if you missed out on a particular freebie. For fans in the US and Canada, the popular [40906](/sets/40906-restaurants-of-the-world-japan) Restaurants of the World: Japan set is returning. You’ll need to spend US$180 or more between July 13-23 to snag it, while stocks last.

Across the pond in the UK and EU, the offer is different. From July 13-16, you can get the [40774](/sets/40774-classic-animation-scenes) Classic Animation Scenes GWP with a minimum spend of £115 or €130. Meanwhile, our friends in Australia and New Zealand get the [40916](/sets/40916-floral-picture-frame) Floral Picture Frame GWP for spending AU$245 or NZD$265 between July 13-23.

There’s also a global offer: a [30731](/sets/30731-tom-nook-and-flying-present) Tom Nook and Flying Present polybag. This one requires a US$50 spend on specific themes like Animal Crossing, Sonic the Hedgehog, Super Mario, The Legend of Zelda, Fortnite, or Minecraft. This offer runs from July 13-23.

The problem for us in India? None of these specific GWPs are listed for our region. While these promotions are running in other parts of the world, Indian fans are left out in the cold. This means the only way to get your hands on these particular GWPs would be through unofficial channels or if you happen to be traveling abroad during the promotion period.

These are gifts with purchase: none of them is sold separately, so there's no retail price to convert. The US$180 figure is the spend needed to get 40906, not its price. MyBrickHouse and Toycra don't stock these promotions, and availability in India is currently none.

It’s a bit of a bummer when these promotions are geographically restricted. We’ll have to keep our eyes peeled for any potential local offers or hope that some of these GWPs eventually make their way to India through official channels, though that seems unlikely based on this announcement. For now, it’s a case of watching from the sidelines.

Verdict: IMPORT ONLY. Not in Indian stores — grey market or wait.

