Beyond these specific set promotions, there are also general spend-based GWPs. Globally, you can get a [30730](/sets/30730-trainer-supplies) Trainer Supplies polybag when you spend US$40 (or local equivalent) on a range of themes including One Piece, City, and NINJAGO. Another global offer sees the [30733](/sets/30733-badnik-skorp) Badnik: Skorp polybag free with a US$40 spend on themes like Sonic the Hedgehog, Super Mario, and Minecraft.

Australian fans get an extra perk: spending AU$325 or more on LEGO.com can net you the [40913](/sets/40913-vintage-parade-car) Icons Vintage Parade Car GWP, but you’ll need to use exclusive promo codes, which are quite limited. These codes stack with other offers, meaning you could potentially grab both Grond and the Vintage Parade Car if you’re strategic.

